# -*- coding: utf-8 -*-
"""
spec_text_en.py —— “i” 按钮里的格式说明（英文版）

★ 2026-10-24：`plan.spec_text()` 原来只返回中文；英文界面下这些弹窗仍是中文。
  这里放同结构的英文版，`spec_text()` 按 `i18n.is_en()` 挑一份。
  文档里的植物 / 僵尸名一律官方英文名，轨道符号与 JSON 字段原样保留。
"""

SPEC_EN = {
    "plan": "# TrackCheck solution JSON format spec (format = trackcheck-plan/3)\n\n## Top level\n\n```json\n{\n  \"format\": \"trackcheck-plan/3\",\n  \"name\": \"Radio Clock No Cobs\",\n  \"note\": \"human-readable note\",\n  \"field\": \"PE\",\n  \"deck\": [\"Ice-shroom\",\"Imitator:Ice-shroom\",\"Doom-shroom\",\"Cherry Bomb\",\"Jalapeno\",\"Squash\",\"Puff-shroom\",\"Flower Pot\",\"Pumpkin\",\"Coffee Bean\"],\n  \"rhythm\": {\"system\":\"C\",\"id\":\"C4io\",\"beats\":[\"N\",\"AA'\",\"I\",\"I\"]},\n  \"waves\":        [ ... ],\n  \"globals\":      [ ... ],\n  \"rescue_simple\":{ ... },\n  \"rescue\":       [ ... ],\n  \"slots\":        { ... },\n  \"params\":       { ... }\n}\n```\n\n- `field`: field code, `PE` (default) / `FE` / `DE` / `NE` / `RE`.\n  It decides the row count, cell height, y coordinate, water lanes, day/night (whether mushrooms sleep), heavy fog, graves, slopes,\n  planting base (Lily Pad on water / Flower Pot on roof) and **zombies banned from spawning**.\n- `deck`: 10 cards. Available are all **48** plants of the original game (including Gold Magnet) + `Imitator`;\n  **Imitator must be written as a two-level object**, like `\"Imitator:Ice-shroom\"` (= the old notation “Imitate Ice-shroom”).\n  What the current engine really knows is: Ice-shroom / Doom-shroom / Cherry Bomb / Jalapeno / Squash / Puff-shroom / Flower Pot /\n  Pumpkin / Garlic / Coffee Bean / Fume-shroom / Gloom-shroom / Winter Melon / Cattail / Lily Pad / Umbrella Leaf / Twin Sunflower /\n  **Cob Cannon / Spikeweed / Spikerock / Tall-nut / Split Pea / Gatling Pea / Torchwood / Magnet-shroom /\n  Blover / Grave Buster**, plus `Imitator:Ice-shroom`, `Imitator:Doom-shroom`;\n  the remaining cards can be selected and written, but the run will log “unknown card”.\n- The `aim` of `Cob Cannon` is the **explosion centre** (any row, **both row and column accept one decimal place**, e.g. `[3, 7.5]`),\n  not “where it is planted”. P does not name a specific cob — the engine automatically picks the one that “is loaded and has the shortest remaining CD”,\n  each cob has its own independent 3475cs timer; **the release-to-explosion delay is ignored** (it explodes the moment it is written).\n- `rhythm.id` is the **canonical id** of the rhythm type (`C4io` / `N4` / `D5` / `I6` …).\n  The display name switches between **2021 traditional / 2026 new / dual-track** per “Settings → Rhythm naming”,\n  so the JSON only stores the id, never the display name.\n- Everywhere below, “what to plant” is written as a **plant name**, not “click ice bank / refill ice bank”:\n  - wake ice bank = **plant a Coffee Bean** in that cell\n  - refill ice bank = **plant an Ice-shroom** in that cell\n  - check ice bank = check the **number of Ice-shrooms on the field** (plant_count) or **what plant is in a cell** (cell_is)\n\n## Mushroom sleep (user ruling 2026-10-22)\n\n- **Mushrooms already in the formation layout are awake and stay awake forever**: Gloom-shroom / Fume-shroom / Magnet-shroom … these resident mushrooms work as usual.\n- **The Ice-shrooms in the formation layout are asleep** (that is what “ice bank” means).\n- **A newly planted mushroom is always asleep** — day or night; to make it work you must, in the **same cell**,\n  plant another `Coffee Bean` (`Coffee Bean` block + `aim` = that cell).\n- **A mushroom that has been woken stays awake forever**, it will not fall back asleep on schedule.\n- So “freeze on planting” and “explode on planting” are both impossible in this model: it sleeps first, then a Coffee Bean wakes it.\n\n## Rhythm (rhythm)\n\n```json\n\"rhythm\": {\"system\": \"C\", \"id\": \"P4\", \"beats\": [\"P\",\"P\",\"P\",\"P\"],\n            \"gaps\": [9, 9, 9, 9], \"pair\": \"auto\"}\n```\n\n- `beats` is the community shorthand track, separated by `|`; “Quick layout” lays it out cyclically over\n  the regular waves w2~w20 (skipping Flag Waves w10/w20), filling in only “what to do”; landing spot / timing / fallback are left blank.\n- `gaps` is the **wavelength list** (seconds): the interval from each beat → the next wave spawn. In the UI write `(9,9,9,9)` or `(9|9|9|9)`.\n- `pair` decides **whether a symmetric operation is written once or as a pair**:\n  - `\"auto\"` (default): two consecutive Ps (`PP`) count as full notation, otherwise shorthand\n  - `\"short\"` shorthand: `P|P|P|P` = 4 pairs of cobs (8 cobs)\n  - `\"full\"` full notation: only `PP|PP|PP|PP` is a pair, `P` = a single cob\n\n### Separators the track understands\n\n| Char | Name | What Quick layout does with it |\n|---|---|---|\n| `|` | isolation mark (wave change) | next beat |\n| `-` | refresh mark (second timing in the same wave) | another block group in the same wave, trigger = `after`, **time left blank** |\n| `/` | split mark (upper and lower half simultaneously) | both operation groups go into the same timing, all landing spots left blank; the split itself already means “a pair”, so it is not doubled by shorthand |\n| `~` | oscillation mark (two rhythms swinging) | both sets are laid in, **alternating cycle by cycle** |\n\nAlphabet: AA' = Cherry Bomb + Jalapeno; N = Doom-shroom; N' = Imitator Doom-shroom; A' = Jalapeno; A = Cherry Bomb; I' = Imitator Ice-shroom; I = Ice-shroom; W = Squash; K = Coffee Bean; C' = Flower Pot; C = Puff-shroom; P = Cob Cannon; Nuke = Doom-shroom; Ice = Ice-shroom; Cherry = Cherry Bomb; Chili = Jalapeno; S = separated cob; D = interception cob (delayed cob)\n\n### Wavelength validation (checked as soon as `gaps` is filled)\n\n- With P: wavelength sum ≥ **36s**; 34~35s is the limit (warning); < 34s is outright impossible\n- With long-CD cards (Ash / ice, card CD 50s): wavelength sum ≥ **54s**, otherwise a warning\n- From that, derive “how many cobs this cycle needs at minimum”: `ceil(shots ÷ (wavelength sum ÷ 34.75s))`\n  — e.g. `I-PP|I-PP|N|PP(18,18,9,9)`: 54s ≈ 1.55 cob CDs, 6 P shots → **4 cobs** are enough\n- It also checks “after the wavelength sum has elapsed, can the cycle's first operation be used again”\n\n## Surface track (waves[])\n\n```json\n{\"w\": 5, \"note\": \"\",\n  \"sets\": [\n    {\"when\": {\"kind\":\"all\",\"of\":[\n                 {\"kind\":\"card_ready\",\"card\":\"Doom-shroom\"},\n                 {\"kind\":\"card_ready_within\",\"card\":\"Cherry Bomb\",\"waves\":0.9},\n                 {\"kind\":\"kernel_slack\",\"cmp\":\">=\",\"value\":0}]},\n     \"ops\": [\n       {\"op\":\"Doom-shroom\",\"aim\":[5,8],\"trig\":{\"kind\":\"spawn\"}},\n       {\"op\":\"Ice-shroom\",\"aim\":[3,2],\"trig\":{\"kind\":\"card\",\"name\":\"Ice-shroom\",\"offset\":0}}\n     ]},\n    {\"when\": {\"kind\":\"always\"}, \"ops\": [ ... ]}\n  ]}\n```\n\n`sets` is the **candidate fallback chain**: the first candidate from the top whose `when` holds wins (= if / elif / else).\n`ops` is the **block sequence**: the first block = immediately on spawn, the following ones rely on triggers.\n\n- `op` may only be: Doom-shroom, Imitator Doom-shroom, Cherry Bomb, Jalapeno, Ice-shroom, Imitator Ice-shroom, Coffee Bean, Squash, Puff-shroom, Flower Pot, Sun-shroom, Scaredy-shroom, Pumpkin, Garlic, Fume-shroom, Gloom-shroom, Lily Pad, Umbrella Leaf, Twin Sunflower, Cob Cannon, Spikeweed, Spikerock, Tall-nut, Split Pea, Gatling Pea, Torchwood, Magnet-shroom, Blover, Grave Buster\n- `aim` = `[row, column]` (row 1~6, column 1~9); if omitted the default strategy is used\n- Trigger `trig.kind` may only be: spawn, time, after, card, dist, state, since, after_block, all, any, not\n  - `spawn` immediately on spawn | `time{\"at\":cs}` time within the wave | `after{\"at\":cs}` after the previous block\n  - `card{\"name\":\"Ice-shroom\",\"offset\":0}` the card CD has finished\n  - `dist{\"zombie\":\"Gargantuar\",\"row\":6,\"col\":6,\"axis\":\"x\",\"cmp\":\"<=\",\"value\":160}` distance\n  - `state{\"what\":\"sun\",\"cmp\":\">=\",\"value\":100}` field state\n- Loop: add `\"repeat\": {\"every\": 100, \"times\": 3}` to a block (`times` omitted = loop forever)\n- Condition `when.kind` may only be: spawn, time, after, card, dist, state, since, after_block, all, any, not, card_ready, card_ready_within, plant_count, cell_is, kernel_slack, prev, always\n  - `prev{\"back\":1,\"target\":\"act\",\"op\":\"Cherry Bomb\"}` = the previous wave **really fired** the Cherry Bomb\n    (`target:\"set\"` looks at “which candidate was selected”; `\"negate\":true` negates it)\n\n## Global checks (globals[])\n\n```json\n{\"id\":\"Refill ice bank\",\"enabled\":true,\"every\":50,\"cooldown\":0,\n  \"when\": {\"kind\":\"card_ready\",\"card\":\"Ice-shroom\"},\n  \"ops\":  [{\"op\":\"Ice-shroom\",\"aim\":[3,2]}]}\n```\nEvery tick the condition is checked once; if it holds the ops are done in order (if one block fails midway, this round is abandoned).\n`every` = how many cs between checks (0 = check every tick).\n\n## Simple rescue (rescue_simple)\n\n```json\n{\"enabled\": true,\n  \"resources\": [{\"op\":\"Puff-shroom\"},{\"op\":\"Squash\"},{\"op\":\"Coffee Bean\",\"aim\":[3,2]}],\n  \"targets\": [\n    {\"id\":\"2-6 Gloom-shroom\",\"protect\":{\"row\":2,\"col\":6},\n      \"urgency_cells\":0,\"priority\":100,\"cooldown\":60}]}\n```\n- `resources`: the resources handed to the rescue handler, tried in order; if one cannot be used, move to the next\n- `targets[].protect`: the cell to protect\n- `urgency_cells`: how many cells away the zombies are when rescue starts (0 = only when on top of it; 1 = one cell away)\n- `priority`: who gets rescued first when several are in danger (larger value first)\n\n## Detailed rescue (rescue[])\n\n```json\n{\"id\":\"Padding\",\"cooldown\":10,\n  \"event\": {\"kind\":\"zombie_in_window\",\"rows\":[6,5,1],\"col\":6,\n             \"window\":[10,75],\"min_hp\":500,\"zombie\":\"any\"},\n  \"levels\": [[{\"op\":\"Puff-shroom\"}], [{\"op\":\"Flower Pot\"}], [{\"op\":\"Squash\"}]]}\n```\n`levels` is the fallback layer: whichever level all lands, it stops. `event.kind` may only be: zombie_in_window, heavy_near_core, bare_core_threat, cell_threat, plant_count, wave, always\n\n## Natural language → JSON (for AI use)\n\n> “w5: if the Doom-shroom is ready and both Cherry Bomb and Jalapeno are ready, click the Doom-shroom at 5-8 first; otherwise fire Cherry Bomb and Jalapeno together; if neither works, click the ice bank”\n```json\n{\"w\":5,\"sets\":[\n  {\"when\":{\"kind\":\"all\",\"of\":[{\"kind\":\"card_ready\",\"card\":\"Doom-shroom\"},\n      {\"kind\":\"card_ready\",\"card\":\"Cherry Bomb\"},{\"kind\":\"card_ready\",\"card\":\"Jalapeno\"}]},\n   \"ops\":[{\"op\":\"Doom-shroom\",\"aim\":[5,8]}]},\n  {\"when\":{\"kind\":\"all\",\"of\":[{\"kind\":\"card_ready\",\"card\":\"Cherry Bomb\"},\n      {\"kind\":\"card_ready\",\"card\":\"Jalapeno\"}]},\n   \"ops\":[{\"op\":\"Cherry Bomb\",\"aim\":[2,8]},{\"op\":\"Jalapeno\"}]},\n  {\"when\":{\"kind\":\"always\"},\"ops\":[{\"op\":\"Coffee Bean\",\"aim\":[3,2]}]}]}\n```\n\n> “Eight cobs P4: one pair of cobs at column 8 every wave, wavelength 9 seconds”\n```json\n{\"rhythm\":{\"id\":\"P4\",\"beats\":[\"P\",\"P\",\"P\",\"P\"],\n            \"gaps\":[9,9,9,9],\"pair\":\"auto\"},\n  \"waves\":[{\"w\":2,\"sets\":[{\"when\":{\"kind\":\"always\"},\"ops\":[\n      {\"op\":\"Cob Cannon\",\"aim\":[3,8],\"trig\":{\"kind\":\"spawn\"}},\n      {\"op\":\"Cob Cannon\",\"aim\":[4,8],\"trig\":{\"kind\":\"spawn\"}}]}]}]}\n```\n(with `pair:\"short\"` writing a single P automatically becomes two cobs; the above is the equivalent “write both blocks yourself” form)\n\n## Cob kinds P / S / D (the block's `cob` field)\n\n| `cob` | Name | Meaning |\n|---|---|---|\n| `P` | regular cob | a pair of cobs bombing columns 8/9; the landing spot may slide |\n| `S` | separated cob | a single finishing cob; **you must fill the landing spot yourself** |\n| `D` | interception cob (delayed cob) | the landing spot is **solved at run time** from “kill every Imp a Gargantuar throws in mid-air” |\n\n`P` / `S` / `D` are all `Cob Cannon`; only the landing spot differs:\n\n- `P` writes `aim` as `[row, \"front\"]`; the engine reads \"front\" as “the front-most zombie of that row”, sliding allowed.\n- `S` leaves `aim` empty (`null`) and waits for you to fill in a concrete `[row, col]`.\n- `D` writes `aim` as `[row, \"imp\"]`, together with `trig`:\n\n```json\n{\"op\":\"Cob Cannon\",\"cob\":\"D\",\"aim\":[2,\"imp\"],\n \"imp_group\":\"low\",\"imp_when\":\"apex\",\n \"trig\":{\"kind\":\"imp\",\"group\":\"low\",\"when\":\"apex\"}}\n```\n\n  - `trig.kind = \"imp\"`: fire only when **an Imp is flying** (if none is in the air it keeps waiting and gives up once the window is gone).\n  - `imp_group`: `low` covers lanes 1~3, `high` covers 4~6 (lanes 4~5 on a 5-lane field), `any` does not split.\n  - `imp_when`: `release` intercept at the throw / `apex` at the highest point (default) / `land` just before landing.\n  - A solution containing `D` or an `imp` trigger enables the “materialised Imp” model (thrown at half HP, flies, and only merges into the body HP on landing); solutions without `D` keep the old model (the Imp merges the instant the Gargantuar dies), so old results are unaffected.\n\n## `wear` in the array (constant wear)\n\nEach cell of the array editor has a “constant wear” checkbox (JSON: `\"wear\": true`).\nIt does two things: (1) automatic deck building brings that plant; (2) an automatic global check “replant whenever needed” is added.\nPlants under a Pumpkin and all purple cards automatically count as `core`, and the rescue layer protects them first.\n\n## In this model an “operation” comes in only two kinds\n\n1. **P** —— `Cob Cannon`: does not name a specific cob, it only looks at each cob's own 3475cs reload;\n   the explosion R=115 / 1800 **takes effect instantly**, the landing spot may carry one decimal.\n2. **Plant (card)** —— every other op is “plant some plant in some cell”.\n   The instant of planting is the trigger (for “trigger on planting” plants — Cherry Bomb / Jalapeno / Squash / Doom-shroom — no extra plant-to-effect delay is counted).\n\nSo the old version's **special move “Squash crushing a Zomboni” has been removed**: it is just\n`Squash` + `aim:[5,9]` + a “lane 5 Zomboni is N px from 5-9” trigger.\n",
    "spawn": "# TrackCheck spawn list JSON format\n\n```json\n{\"app\":\"trackcheck-spawn\",\n \"jobs\":[{\"name\":\"Slow run (preset)\",\"kinds\":[\"Zombie\",\"Conehead Zombie\",\"Football Zombie\"],\"seeds\":5}]}\n```\n\n- `jobs[]`: a set of spawns to simulate\n- `kinds`: the zombie types allowed to appear (Chinese names, see the checkboxes on the sandbox page)\n- `seeds`: how many runs (1~30)\n- Giving only `{\"jobs\":[...]}` also works, and giving an array directly also works\n",
    "spawnmech": "# TrackCheck · Spawn (refresh) mechanics\n\n> Based on `docs/knowledge-base/02-core-zombie-spawn-mechanics.md` (the four basic rules R0/R1/R2/R3,\n> sources: Tieba thread 5194693832, wiki “Survival Endless Primer” §6(4), old and new readers).\n> **The engine computes by this mechanism, it does not apply the “Operation Count law”** — Operation Count is only the empirical summary of this mechanism from long-term practice.\n\n## The four rules\n\n| No. | Rule | Value |\n|---|---|---|\n| **R0** | spawn wave 1 at a fixed time after entering | **6.0s** |\n| **R0a** | w9/w19: this wave's zombies are all dead **or drag on for 45s** → red words → next wave spawns **7.2s** later | 45s / 7.2s |\n| **R0b** | w20: all dead **or drag on for 49s** → white words → ends **5s** later | 49s / 5s |\n| **R1** | the interval between any two waves is **never less than 6s** | 6.0s |\n| **R2** | this wave's remaining HP / this wave's total HP < **random threshold** → refresh activated, next wave spawns **2s** later | threshold 0.5~0.67 (fixed the instant this wave spawns) |\n| **R3** | each wave additionally rolls a forced refresh time of **25~31s**, spawning on schedule no matter what | 25~31s |\n\nSo the actual wavelength is decided jointly by “**the instant HP drops to the threshold**” and “the R1 lower bound / R3 upper bound”:\n\n```\nwavelength = clamp( R1 6s , HP drops below threshold + 2s , R3 25~31s )\n```\n\n## What this means for “when to fire”\n\n- **A cob does not “fire and therefore refresh”**, it refreshes only when “HP is knocked down to the threshold”.\n  A pair of cobs (2 cobs) usually cannot reach the threshold → this wave keeps grinding on IO until it drops below the threshold.\n- To keep the wavelength steady at 9s, you need **HP to drop to the threshold at ~7s** (+2s spawn vacuum = 9s).\n  That is: **the firing timing has to be hand-computed from “where this wave's zombies are and how much HP they have left”**, there is no shortcut.\n- In early waves (little HP) a pair of cobs alone can push past the threshold → the wavelength will be clearly shorter than 9s; this is the mechanism itself, not a bug.\n\n## How the solution expresses “hand-computed timing”\n\n| Trigger | Usage |\n|---|---|\n| `time` (time within the wave) | takes effect at the N-th cs after this wave spawns |\n| `since` (since some block last took effect) | **cross-wave anchor**: fire N cs after the last “Cob Cannon” took effect — writes the 9s rhythm out directly |\n| `dist` (distance) | how many px a zombie type still is from a cell |\n| `card` (card CD) | N cs after a card becomes ready |\n\nExample: the 9s pair of cobs of P4 ——\n\n```json\n{\"op\":\"Cob Cannon\",\"aim\":[2,8],\"trig\":{\"kind\":\"since\",\"op\":\"Cob Cannon\",\"at\":8800}}\n```\n\n(`at` uses 8800 instead of 9000: after R2 activates there is still a 2s spawn vacuum, actual wavelength ≈ 8.8 + 0.2\n— for a true 9s, fine-tune by measurement.)\n",
    "layout": "# TrackCheck formation layout notes\n\n## Every item in the UI\n\n| Position | Meaning |\n|---|---|\n| Field | PE Pool (day) / FE Fog (night) / DE Day front lawn / NE Night front lawn / RE Roof. Decides row count, cell height, y coordinate, water lanes, day/night, heavy fog, graves, slopes, base and zombies banned from spawning |\n| Formation name | Format `[field].name`, e.g. `[PE].Radio Clock No Cobs`. The `[field].` part is generated by the app automatically, you only fill in the name after it; the prefix follows automatically when you change the field |\n| Main plant | The 45 cards other than Pumpkin / Lily Pad / Flower Pot, plus optionally `Imitator:X` |\n| Awake | **Only mushrooms sleep**. Resident mushrooms preset in the formation count as awake; pending ones such as Ice-shroom / Doom-shroom may be left asleep |\n| Pumpkin | an independent 4000 HP shell layer |\n| Ladder | ladder pumpkin: zombies other than Gargantuar and Zomboni **walk straight over**. **Ladders cannot be placed on water** (the checkbox is locked);\npumpkin must be ticked first, the ladder follows the pumpkin |\n| Lily Pad / Flower Pot | base. **An empty cell may have no base first**; but as long as the cell has a plant, is wearing a pumpkin or has a ladder, the water lanes of PE / FE and the roof of RE must have a base (the UI locks the checkbox on automatically). Grass can only take a Flower Pot, not a Lily Pad |\n| Grave | only appears in NE; Grave Buster can clear it directly |\n\n## Cob Cannon (1×2)\n\nCob Cannon occupies **two cells**: the head cell (the one you click) is the body, the cell **one column to the right, column number +1** is the tail cell.\nThe tail cell is marked “cob tail” on the diagram; nothing can be planted there and no pumpkin can be placed.\n\n- water / roof: **both cells need a base** (Lily Pad / Flower Pot), added automatically when generating the string\n- **cannot wear a pumpkin, cannot take a ladder** (these two checkboxes are locked)\n- column 9 cannot hold a Cob Cannon (the tail cell goes out of bounds)\n\n## JSON (for import/export)\n\n```json\n{\n  \"field\": \"PE\",\n  \"name\": \"Radio Clock No Cobs\",\n  \"array\": {\n    \"1-1\": {\"plant\": \"Gloom-shroom\", \"pumpkin\": true, \"ladder\": false,\n            \"awake\": true, \"base\": null, \"grave\": false},\n    \"3-2\": {\"plant\": \"Ice-shroom\", \"awake\": false, \"base\": \"Lily Pad\"},\n    \"3-4\": {\"plant\": \"Cob Cannon\", \"base\": \"Lily Pad\", \"pumpkin\": false},\n    \"3-5\": {\"plant\": null, \"base\": \"Lily Pad\"}\n  }\n}\n```\n\n- `name` is the **bare formation name** (without `[PE].`), full name = `[` + `field` + `].` + `name`\n- keys are `\"row-column\"`, row 1 at the top and column 1 closest to the house\n- `plant` being `null` means this cell has no main plant (but it may hold only a pumpkin / base / grave)\n- `awake: false` is only an “asleep” marker, `Ice-shroom + awake:false` ≡ the engine's internal “ice bank”\n- **base rule** (`base`): on water only `Lily Pad`, on roof/grass only `Flower Pot`;\n  an empty cell may omit `base`; when a plant / `pumpkin` / `ladder` is written or `plant == \"Cob Cannon\"`,\n  cells on water and roof **must** have a `base` (auto-filled when writing the file)\n- **water never has `ladder`**: ladders can only go on pumpkins on land / roof, and are cleared if written in\n- the tail cell of a Cob Cannon is a `plant: null` + `base: \"Lily Pad\"` record in JSON (Flower Pot on the roof)\n\n## PvZ Tools formation string (RFC1437)\n\nClick “Generate string” / “Import” to interoperate with PvZ Tools. Encoding rules:\nBase64 → XOR the whole thing with `0x54` → zlib stream + 1 byte RS (high 4 bits rake row, low 4 bits scene).\nScene codes: 0 day / 1 night / 2 pool / 3 fog / 4 roof / 5 moonlit night.\n16 bits per cell: `P(10~15) PI(9) PA(8) B(6~7) BI(5) K(4) KI(3) C(2) CI(1) L(0)`.\n\n## Notes\n\n- 5-row fields (DE / NE / RE) have only 45 cells, anything in row 6 is ignored\n- Cob Cannon takes **1×2** (the tail cell cannot be planted, cannot wear a pumpkin; both cells need a base on water/roof)\n- an empty cell in the formation may hold just a base (Lily Pad / Flower Pot), or nothing at all\n",
    "resultonly": "# TrackCheck · Overall modelling principle: **result-oriented**\n\nIn the simplified model, “when an operation is finished being written” equals “when the result appears”.\nThe delays below really exist in the original game (`[precise]`, documented),\nbut in this tool they are **never counted**, only kept as comments:\n\n| Item | Original value | This tool |\n|---|---|---|\n| Cob landing spot | the landing spot is the **crosshair**, explosion centre = crosshair x − 7 | **the landing spot is the explosion centre**, no conversion |\n| Cob: fire → explosion | 373~392cs (roof 359~392) | **0** |\n| Cherry Bomb / Jalapeno: placement → effect | 100cs | **0** |\n| Doom-shroom / daytime Ice-shroom: placement → effect | 298~299cs (including Coffee Bean) | **0** |\n| Daytime mushroom: click Coffee Bean → wake | 100cs | **0** |\n| Bullet flight time | each has its own hit delay (pea 34cs etc.) | **bullets are not simulated**, damage settles at the instant of the attack |\n\n## Why do it this way\n\nWhat you need to judge is “**can this track hold up**” — landing spot, timing, whether the Operation Count is enough.\nA bullet flying a few centiseconds, when a Coffee Bean wakes up, only changes the timing at the centisecond level,\nyet it would make “where exactly does the `[2,8]` I wrote explode” hard to predict.\n\n## Exceptions (delays still kept)\n\n- cob **reload** (3475cs, independent per cob) — this is a hard constraint, not a delay\n- **card CD** of Ash / ice (50s) — same reason\n- **duration** of freeze / slow (freeze 400~600cs, slow 1000/2000cs)\n- the split of Gloom-shroom's 4 hits within one round (74/102/130/158cs) — that is its damage structure, not flight time\n",
    "config": "# TrackCheck full config JSON format\n\n```json\n{\"format\":\"trackcheck-config/1\",\n \"spawns\":[{\"name\":\"Slow run\",\"kinds\":[\"Zombie\",\"Conehead Zombie\"],\"seeds\":3,\"planId\":\"p1\"}],\n \"plans\":[{\"id\":\"p1\",\"name\":\"Radio Clock No Cobs\",\"plan\":{ ... trackcheck-plan/3 ... }}]}\n```\n\n- `spawns`: the list in the Spawn Sandbox; `planId` points at `plans[].id` (empty = use the built-in judge track)\n- `plans`: the multiple solutions in the Solution editor; the `plan` field is the complete solution JSON\n- on import, solutions are created first, then the spawns are bound back by `planId`\n",
}
